  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the best result so far at 0.485 accuracy, clearly outperforming image_only/resnet50 (0.208) and rna_only/scgpt (0.411). This establishes PCA-2000 RNA as the strongest single-modality baseline. Uncertainty: We have not yet tested whether multiprofile aggregation can improve upon the single-profile result. This experiment tests config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool), which is a minimal, single-variable extension of the best result—changing only the profile setting from single to multi and adding a simple average-pool aggregation. This isolates the effect of multiprofile on the top RNA encoder. It is the best use of experiment 4 because: (1) it directly extends the strongest configuration, (2) it uses the simplest aggregation (avgpool) before testing more complex ones, (3) the outcome will determine whether to invest remaining budget in multiprofile variants (transformer aggregation, multimodal multiprofile) or pivot to other directions (scvi_n200, better image encoders, multimodal fusion)."
}

